{
  "sn22.60:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.60 ",
  "sn22.60:0.2": "6. Involvement ",
  "sn22.60:0.3": "With Mahāli ",
  "sn22.60:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn22.60:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "sn22.60:1.3": "Then Mahāli the Licchavi went up to the Buddha … and said to him: ",
  "sn22.60:2.1": "“Sir, Pūraṇa Kassapa says this: ",
  "sn22.60:2.2": "‘There is no cause or reason for the corruption of sentient beings. ",
  "sn22.60:2.3": "Sentient beings are corrupted without cause or reason. ",
  "sn22.60:2.4": "There’s no cause or reason for the purification of sentient beings. ",
  "sn22.60:2.5": "Sentient beings are purified without cause or reason.’ ",
  "sn22.60:2.6": "What does the Buddha say about this?” ",
  "sn22.60:3.1": "“Mahāli, there is a cause and reason for the corruption of sentient beings. ",
  "sn22.60:3.2": "Sentient beings are corrupted with cause and reason. ",
  "sn22.60:3.3": "There is a cause and reason for the purification of sentient beings. ",
  "sn22.60:3.4": "Sentient beings are purified with cause and reason.” ",
  "sn22.60:4.1": "“But sir, what is the cause and reason for the corruption of sentient beings? ",
  "sn22.60:4.2": "How are sentient beings corrupted with cause and reason?” ",
  "sn22.60:5.1": "“Mahāli, if form were absolutely painful—soaked and steeped in pain and not steeped in pleasure—sentient beings wouldn’t be aroused by it. ",
  "sn22.60:5.2": "But